{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794193-would-a-city-murder-spirit-be-a-magath","id":794193,"title":"Would a city / murder spirit be a magath?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-28T08:10:47-08:00","id":794193,"title":"Would a city / murder spirit be a magath?","content":"A friend of mine is about to run his first werewolf game, set in Glasgow. The city is meant to be the murder capital of Europe during the game and so the leader of the city spirits in Glasgow is Nanfarthir'dar (the city that kills), a city / murder spirit who is either rank 5 or 6. So my question is the one from the title, would a spirit of murder and cities count as a magath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T08:16:59-08:00","id":794196,"title":"","content":"Is it natural for a city spirit to feed on it's most prominent happenings? If the answer is yes, then the spirit isn't a Magath.<br /> <br /> Magath are unnatural because they feed on things they shouldn't. At all.<br /> <br /> A dog that ate cars. Lava-bees. That sort of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:10:18-08:00","id":794411,"title":"","content":"Probably not. City-fathers as a spirit type are very unusual creatures (not surprisingly once you get to the sort of power, rank and complexity that these spirits have). They frequently include traits that are related to the area that they rule, without it turning them into Magath even when they're strange combinations. Take a look at Shadows over the UK for some examples of just how strange some of these spirits can be. Also as a City spirit, it thematically fits that it would be natural for the spirit to devour anything that has a link to its city, so it should be able to devour murder essence as much as it likes without ever mutating and becoming a Magath.<br /> <br /> That said when it comes to your friend's setting, it's their Chronicle and the idea of a mutated Magath city-father ruling over the spirit courts is an amazingly terrifying concept so if they want to do it... I'd just say go for it. The Spirit world is more art than science and if they say this one spirit worked out as a Magath, then that's perfectly fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T05:20:29-08:00","id":794769,"title":"","content":"I guess it could be a magath if there is something deeply unnatural behind the number of murders that is corrupting the flows and webs of Essence in the city. Perhaps an Abyssal or greater Infernal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:50:22-08:00","id":794862,"title":"","content":"A city that recently fell victim to dereliction, blight, and gentrification would probably be a good candidate, especially if a bunch of big-box stores and distribution centers popped up overnight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T21:48:38-08:00","id":795378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794193-would-a-city-murder-spirit-be-a-magath?p=794196#post794196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dog that ate cars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that what happens when they actually catch them? Huh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T07:59:02-08:00","id":796839,"title":"","content":"A chihuahua / sports-car magath. *yip yip yi-vrroooooom*. Running around the shadow, barking at everything that moves, racing other spirits, leaving skidmarks all over the place and pissing off any kind of spirit that has ears.<br /> <br /> Edit: This magath would take chasing it's own tail to a whole new level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6365,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","user":"Fumus","date":". 12-30-2015, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T04:59:49-08:00","id":801283,"title":"","content":"Lava-bees!?<br /> <br /> Amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T20:28:59-08:00","id":804234,"title":"","content":"I kind of want to see a Tribe (probably a Pure Tribe?) devoted to colluding with Magath.<br /> <br /> Also, a Mage Legacy, because everything needs Mage Legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T20:47:37-08:00","id":804241,"title":"","content":"A whole tribe might be odd, especially with the variety of magath out there. But there's at least one 'canon' magath totem among the Pure, a Lune blended with a Helion, for double the craziness. There's another one, a death spirit that popped up during a festival and ended up eating joy Essence, becoming 'Glad of Killing' and is now riding and urging a human.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'd imagine a Lodge devoted to diplomacy with magath would be more common among the Forsaken, what with the magath sort of being the Forsaken of the spirit world, shunned by all the choirs due to something they did in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-08-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T20:49:48-08:00","id":804982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794193-would-a-city-murder-spirit-be-a-magath?p=804241#post804241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A whole tribe might be odd, especially with the variety of magath out there. But there's at least one 'canon' magath totem among the Pure, a Lune blended with a Helion, for double the craziness. There's another one, a death spirit that popped up during a festival and ended up eating joy Essence, becoming 'Glad of Killing' and is now riding and urging a human.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'd imagine a Lodge devoted to diplomacy with magath would be more common among the Forsaken, what with the magath sort of being the Forsaken of the spirit world, shunned by all the choirs due to something they did in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>What book had this helion / lune magath? I never knew about it but I so need to read about this thing now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:24:26-08:00","id":804997,"title":"","content":"The book doesn't go into detail about it. It's from the Pure book, all it says is, 'The pack\u2019s totem is a Lune magath blended with a Helion into a horrific beast that demands prayers and sacrifices at various hours of the day and night.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T00:09:23-08:00","id":805060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794193-would-a-city-murder-spirit-be-a-magath?p=796839#post796839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A chihuahua / sports-car magath. *yip yip yi-vrroooooom*. Running around the shadow, barking at everything that moves, racing other spirits, leaving skidmarks all over the place and pissing off any kind of spirit that has ears.<br /> <br /> Edit: This magath would take chasing it's own tail to a whole new level.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmmmm the pissing off could be literal for a pissing on.......when he tries to mark the tree spirits ...naturally with fuel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T01:02:03-08:00","id":805072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794193-would-a-city-murder-spirit-be-a-magath?p=804997#post804997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book doesn't go into detail about it. It's from the Pure book, all it says is, 'The pack\u2019s totem is a Lune magath blended with a Helion into a horrific beast that demands prayers and sacrifices at various hours of the day and night.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, that's disappointing. The art that a lune/helion would be amazing to see. I'm picturing like the crescent moon crane that predators has as an example for ithalunims who flickers constantly between firey and glowing silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T01:03:24-08:00","id":805074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794193-would-a-city-murder-spirit-be-a-magath?p=805060#post805060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmm the pissing off could be literal for a pissing on.......when he tries to mark the tree spirits ...naturally with fuel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Marks his territory, with the petrol pump hose on his under carriage, a helion comes along and winds up setting the area ablaze by accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}